	default 103200
	help
	  lll_conn_isr_rx's path to radio_pkt_tx_set()'s RESPOND store:
	  silicon 103.2 us (Peripheral), QEMU 133.0 us (Peripheral; Central
	  121.2 us). With EFR32_RADIO_CONN_STAGED the same store commits the
	  reply the sequencer sent and re-arms the RX FIFO (7.82).

# Link-layer AES-CCM on RADIOAES (crypto/radioaes.c, docs/crypto.md), for encrypted connections:
# the completion job decrypts each received PDU before the LLL callback and the callback (or a
# Central's prepare) encrypts the next. The connection figures above were measured without
# encryption, so these are added to them where encryption runs (include/hal/efr32/ll_deadlines.h).
# Silicon: tests/crypto-port on the BGM220 explorer kit, HCLK 76.8 MHz, the call through
# efr32_radioaes_ccm() with interrupts locked, longest of 64 (DWT). QEMU: the same test in
# build/qemu. With data length extension a PDU carries up to 251 octets, else 27.

config EFR32_RADIO_CONN_COMPLETION_TO_STAGED_NS
	int "Connection receive completion: start to the next stage posted (ns)"
	default 67700 if EFR32_RADIO_TIMING_QEMU
	default 95100
	help
	  With EFR32_RADIO_CONN_STAGED: longest path from a connection
	  receive's completion start (isr_rx(), committing the sequencer's
	  outcome) to the replies to the next receive staged
	  (efr32_radio_conn_stage()), unencrypted; an encrypted link adds two
	  encryptions and one accelerator wait (ll_deadlines.h).
	  Silicon 95.1 us (a held 5-minute connection, 7.84; replaces 7.82's
	  provisional 46.1 us from a few events). 7.82: silicon 46.1 us (Peripheral, host
	  Central, few events: PROVISIONAL until a held silicon connection),
	  QEMU 67.7 us (Peripheral; Central 33.9 us).

